## Background

HarnessAgent skipped telemetry dispatch when no explicit telemetry options were supplied, even if integrations had been registered globally through `registerTelemetry()`

This made global telemetry registration inconsistent with generateText, streamText and ToolLoopAgent. Users had to configure telemetry directly on the harness agent to receive lifecycle events.

Before: individual telemetry had to be defined
```ts
const agent = new HarnessAgent({
  harness,
  telemetry: {
    integrations: [integration],
  },
});
```

## Summary

Always create the harness telemetry dispatcher so globally registered integrations receive lifecycle events without per-call configuration.

After: 
```ts
import { registerTelemetry } from 'ai';
import { HarnessAgent } from '@ai-sdk/harness/agent';

registerTelemetry({
  onStart() {
    console.log('Generation started');
  },
  onEnd() {
    console.log('Generation finished');
  },
});

const agent = new HarnessAgent({ harness });
```

